{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve had this left flank pain for about a week. My urine’s been cloudy, and I’ve felt nauseous. No fever though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You mentioned your Foley catheter was replaced a week ago—have you changed it since then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not since. I didn’t get around to it. I’ve also had some left lower belly pain and constipation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you said you felt dizzy when standing up yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, just for a second. I also had a drink yesterday after not drinking for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ll keep that in mind. You were recently diagnosed with a blood clot in your right leg and started on Coumadin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, but I didn’t fill that prescription. I just didn’t get to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important—we’ll need to restart that. Your INR was low when you came in, so we’re giving you a shot of Lovenox to bridge you while we restart Coumadin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try to keep up with it this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also gave you an IV antibiotic in the ER—Meropenem—for your suspected kidney infection. We’ll switch you to IV Ceftriaxone soon based on your past cultures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it from my bladder again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely, yes. Your urine test showed bacteria and white blood cells. We sent a culture, and it came back with E. coli, which is common in these cases."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need antibiotics for long?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, about 10 days. We’ll start IV and switch to oral Cefpodoxime later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed a metabolic acidosis in your blood work. We’re giving you IV fluids, and it’s already improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was mild and resolved quickly with fluids. Nothing to worry about now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also placed a temporary line in your left groin for IV access since your arms are hard to use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2188-12-16 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s a bit sore, but okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2188-12-17 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your pain seems a bit worse in the lower left belly. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2188-12-17 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it’s more bloated, and I haven’t passed gas. The pain’s sharper now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2188-12-17 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re concerned about possible bowel obstruction. We’ll get an X-ray and possibly a CT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2188-12-17 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like a blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2188-12-17 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but your X-ray shows a lot of stool but no blockage. We’ll do a CT to be sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2188-12-18 21:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT is back. No bowel obstruction. You have a lot of retained stool—severe constipation. That’s likely causing your pain and bloating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2188-12-18 21:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve been taking my senna."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2188-12-18 21:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes with neurogenic bowel, you need more aggressive treatment. We’re going to place a nasogastric tube to help decompress your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2188-12-18 21:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds awful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2188-12-18 21:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s uncomfortable, but it’ll help relieve the pressure. We got 400 cc out right away, and you’re already less distended."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2188-12-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your belly is less tender, and you’ve started passing stool. Surgery was consulted but agreed it’s constipation, not a surgical issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2188-12-19 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2188-12-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a manual disimpaction yesterday and started you on polyethylene glycol. You’ve had good output since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2188-12-19 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess I let it go too long again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2188-12-19 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It happens. We’ll make sure you have a strong bowel regimen at discharge to prevent this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2188-12-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture also grew Enterococcus, but it’s not resistant, and the antibiotics cover it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2188-12-20 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that worse than E. coli?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2188-12-20 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not really. Both are common in catheter-related infections. Your treatment covers both."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2188-12-20 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is improving with Coumadin. You’ll need to get it checked regularly after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2188-12-20 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2188-12-20 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your primary care doctor will arrange it. We’ve scheduled your first check for early next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned the shelter is your plan. We’ve arranged your medications and follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take Cefpodoxime twice a day for four more days. Continue your Metformin, and we’ve added daily MiraLAX and extra stool softeners."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the blood thinner?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, Warfarin 3 mg daily. Do not miss doses. Get your INR checked as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep up with your bowel routine—senna at night, MiraLAX daily. Preventing constipation is key."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. It’s hard to stay on top of everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. That’s why we’ve simplified your meds and set up follow-up. Call your doctor if you have fever, pain, or swelling in your leg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. A nurse will go over everything before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—my pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can take acetaminophen as needed. We’re keeping your gabapentin and amitriptyline the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my antidepressant?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We lowered your fluoxetine to 20 mg daily. Take two capsules. Let your psychiatrist know how you feel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also send you with suppositories in case you get backed up again. Use them as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep them handy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—avoid alcohol while on Warfarin and antibiotics. It can increase side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I know. I just had one drink. Won’t happen again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not judging. Just want you safe. Take care, and follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The nurse will be in shortly with your prescriptions and instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2188-12-21 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2188-12-16 11:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2188-12-21 14:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of paraplegia, neurogenic bladder, and chronic Foley catheter use was admitted with left flank pain, cloudy urine, and nausea, diagnosed with acute pyelonephritis due to E. coli, and treated with IV meropenem followed by ceftriaxone and transitioned to oral cefpodoxime. She also presented with constipation causing abdominal pain and distension, which worsened and required NG tube decompression and manual disimpaction, with subsequent improvement on aggressive bowel regimen. Her INR was subtherapeutic for her known right leg DVT, so she was bridged with Lovenox and restarted on warfarin with outpatient monitoring arranged. Metabolic acidosis resolved with IV fluids. She was discharged to a shelter with medication adjustments, including continued warfarin, antibiotics, and enhanced bowel regimen, with close follow-up for INR and primary care.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pyelonephritis without lesion of renal medullary necrosis",
      "Paraplegia",
      "Acidosis",
      "Other impaction of intestine",
      "Escherichia coli [E. coli] infection in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site",
      "Streptococcus infection in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site, streptococcus, group D [Enterococcus]",
      "Diabetes with unspecified complication, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Orthostatic hypotension",
      "Chronic pain syndrome",
      "Neurogenic bladder NOS",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Other and unspecified alcohol dependence, continuous",
      "Cannabis abuse, unspecified",
      "Incontinence of feces",
      "Cocaine abuse, unspecified",
      "Late effects of injuries due to legal intervention",
      "Below knee amputation status",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Other postprocedural status"
    ]
  }
}
